se that will lead  to perhaps other discoveries does this  open a new pathway or is this just a  great new development in immunotherapy  use well you know classically in cancer  we start drugs in the end stage of  disease you know where people are  failing failed everything and then we  see if it helps  immunotherapy had some benefit there and  this is moving it upfront so it's going  to benefit large numbers of patients  and what we're seeing now is it is  betting multiple we call it body types  so other kinds of cancer bladder cancer  melanoma kidney cancer we're seeing  benefit and we're seeing more there are  literally hundreds of clinical trials  ongoing now across the country seeing  how can we use it in other types of  cancer but this is hope on the frontier  it's not a cure but it is offering a  long-term and well tolerated therapy  that can actually lengthen people's  lives who you talk about lengthening  people's lives without getting too ahead  of ourselves could we possibly be  looking at cures in the near future  you know the c-word curing cancer is  something we shy away from and so my  goal is to make people live a long and  quality life while not having a lot of  side effects from the treatment and  that's where we're going now so cure is  something that we certainly dream of but  I don't think we're there yet but  lengthening life in a quality way we're  seeing that with this drug all right  promising the new discoveries thank you  dr. agus
 

